# Content comes from the Carmela content sheet

- `src/data/events.generated.ts` and `src/data/artists.generated.ts` are GENERATED by `pnpm import-content`.
  Never edit them by hand, and never add events or artists in code: the change would be overwritten on the next import.
  To change content, the sheet changes; then run `pnpm import-content` and review `git diff src/data`.
- `src/data/artists.ts` only re-exports `ARTISTS` and the `a(id)` lookup. `events.generated.ts` uses `a('id')` in lineups.
- The `Event` / `Artist` shapes in `@/types/index` are the contract. If a type gets a new field, add the column
  to the sheet and map it in `scripts/import-content.ts` (look for `readTab(wb, 'Events'` and the `const e` object).

## Media conventions (the import derives every path, nothing is typed)

- Event folder name = event `id`: `public/events/<id>/`
- Flyer: `public/events/<id>/flyer.png` (or `.jpg` / `.webp`)
- Main video (optional, replaces the flyer as main media): `public/events/<id>/video.mp4`
- Footage (optional): every image/video in `public/events/<id>/footage/`, in alphabetical order; heights are read from the files.
- Artist photos: `public/images/artists/<file>`, file name comes from the sheet.

## When asked to "add an event" from pasted text

Don't edit the generated files. Instead, turn the text into rows for the sheet (Events tab, lineup in its Set N / Note N columns using artist names;
Artists tab for new artists), reuse existing artist ids from `artists.generated.ts`, and tell the user what to paste where.
